    "GT23: the E01/E02 table files and the Q01 v2 observations.jsonl that v11 was built from were deleted on 2026-11-25 (disk cleanup approved by Jose). GT23 v12 therefore reads the v11 PACKAGE (full_phase/full_time and assessment.jsonl, hash-checked against its manifest) instead of the E01/E02 inputs; v11 power values are already the D-REF-5 values so the power transform is not applied again. GT21 and UM21 read the same source inputs as v1 and v5.",
    "Shared builder contributor_tools/common/release_package.py gained an additive, opt-in rule: a part that is itself a package table (carries source_export etc.) has those columns dropped on read and per-row source_export labels kept (strip_extra / package_input). Schemas without them behave exactly as before; the three older runner tests pass.",
    "Implemented as thin NEW adapter files (run_gt23_r01_bundle_v12.py, run_gt21_r01_package_v2.py, run_um21_r01_package_v6.py) that import the previous runners unedited, so v11/v1/v5 receipt bindings stay valid (UM21 v5 precedent); the shared logic is contributor_tools/common/foot_flat.py and foot_flat_adapter.py.",
    "Attempt history kept as evidence: GT23 a1/a2 stopped at input checks (deleted files), a3 failed only the G6 check on a pilot subset, a4 ran clean in content but its receipt is unclean because I edited bound files during the run (bindings_unchanged false); GT21 a2 and a3 failed (angle_range None; FF5 wording), a4 superseded by a later code change; UM21 a1 failed (method name clash); readback GT21 first run hit the 768 MiB address-space cap and was rewritten to read a few columns per pass. All final gating pilots, full builds and readbacks have clean receipts.",
    "GT23 ankle L1 failures grow: observations with ankle samples beyond +50 degrees go from 9 to 24 (the -6.7 degree median offset adds about +6.7 degrees to ankle dorsiflexion); 17 phase and 7 time observations became failed, 21 phase and 2 time recovered (all CoP L5). Not tuned; reported as found.",
    "Rotated CoP samples outside the coarse CoP limits: counted in evidence/foot_flat_transform_check.csv (not masked; the dataset CoP masks were applied before the shift and are unchanged). UM21 time table carries no L1/L5 assessment, so its CoP is not limit-checked.",
    "Free disk after the three builds: 19 GiB (launcher floor 15 GiB). Nothing was deleted; failed and superseded pilot roots are still on disk."
